1
00:00:14,460 --> 00:00:15,830
<i>The spirits...</i>

2
00:00:18,250 --> 00:00:20,960
<i>If only I could see them too.</i>

3
00:00:37,580 --> 00:00:39,040
<i>A spirit?</i>

4
00:00:40,130 --> 00:00:41,170
Gadiel.

5
00:00:41,250 --> 00:00:42,290
Yes?

6
00:00:42,580 --> 00:00:45,710
We cannot form pacts with spirits.

7
00:00:45,790 --> 00:00:48,500
It's been a long-standing
mystery of the royal family.

8
00:00:48,710 --> 00:00:51,080
And since we are unable
to receive their blessings,

9
00:00:51,670 --> 00:00:54,210
we have no choice but to rely
on the Vankreift family.

10
00:00:55,170 --> 00:00:56,750
Yes, Your Majesty.

11
00:01:04,670 --> 00:01:05,830
Everything's fine.

12
00:01:05,920 --> 00:01:09,000
It looks like Ellen safely made
it back to the spirit castle.

13
00:01:10,290 --> 00:01:11,960
I'm so glad.

14
00:01:12,040 --> 00:01:15,290
Nevertheless, she'll be getting
an earful once we get home.

15
00:02:46,130 --> 00:02:50,080
FEUD BETWEEN THE ROYAL FAMILY AND THE SPIRITS

16
00:02:51,670 --> 00:02:54,330
Ori, would you mind hanging back a bit?

17
00:02:54,750 --> 00:02:55,790
All right.

18
00:03:00,330 --> 00:03:02,710
I saw your daughter wasn't in attendance.

19
00:03:02,790 --> 00:03:06,540
My apologies. She isn't feeling very well.

20
00:03:06,830 --> 00:03:08,750
No need to lie to my face.

21
00:03:09,080 --> 00:03:12,710
It's a shame. I was hoping
to introduce my sons.

22
00:03:13,170 --> 00:03:14,750
Oh, and...

23
00:03:17,000 --> 00:03:20,830
Things have gotten quite
interesting with the bride.

24
00:03:24,540 --> 00:03:27,670
Indeed. Sauvel is one lucky man,

25
00:03:28,210 --> 00:03:31,790
to be able to marry a woman
as wonderful as her.

26
00:03:33,830 --> 00:03:35,790
Well, I'm glad.

27
00:03:36,210 --> 00:03:41,130
I shall await you and your daughter
at my castle a week from now.

28
00:03:41,420 --> 00:03:43,250
I will allow you to meet my sons.

29
00:03:43,960 --> 00:03:46,630
Now then, if you'll excuse me...

30
00:03:57,750 --> 00:03:59,380
P-Please wait!

31
00:03:59,460 --> 00:04:00,580
Just let me through!

32
00:04:03,500 --> 00:04:05,210
Brother dearest...

33
00:04:07,540 --> 00:04:08,960
You there, leave us.

34
00:04:09,040 --> 00:04:10,080
What?

35
00:04:10,170 --> 00:04:12,420
I'm here, so it'll be all right.

36
00:04:20,420 --> 00:04:22,290
Explain yourself!

37
00:04:22,380 --> 00:04:24,580
Dear, you mustn't be violent.

38
00:04:25,500 --> 00:04:28,540
You look like you haven't the slightest clue.

39
00:04:28,790 --> 00:04:33,040
Because of you, the royal family's
set their sights on Ellen!

40
00:04:34,290 --> 00:04:35,880
Because of me?

41
00:04:35,960 --> 00:04:39,880
That's right. You've been
condemned by Goddess Vár.

42
00:04:40,960 --> 00:04:43,880
Not only that, the royal family knows!

43
00:04:43,960 --> 00:04:48,710
Do you realize the terrible position
this puts the Vankreift family in?!

44
00:04:48,790 --> 00:04:51,000
That's enough, dear.

45
00:04:54,460 --> 00:04:59,170
I understand your rage is because
you love me and Ellen so much.

46
00:04:59,250 --> 00:05:00,210
But...

47
00:05:00,290 --> 00:05:02,500
We just got unlucky this time.

48
00:05:03,000 --> 00:05:06,920
Meanwhile, it seems that blackhearted man
has frustratingly <i>good</i> luck.

49
00:05:07,170 --> 00:05:08,880
What will Ellen say?

50
00:05:08,960 --> 00:05:13,330
Goodness, she'll be fine.
She's our child, after all.

51
00:05:13,830 --> 00:05:17,290
I'm certain she'll find a way
to surprise everyone.

52
00:05:17,630 --> 00:05:19,380
Just like she did here, no?

53
00:05:22,000 --> 00:05:25,830
Now, Aria... do you have the courage
to offer up your daughter

54
00:05:25,920 --> 00:05:27,960
for a crime someone else committed?

55
00:05:28,250 --> 00:05:29,210
What?

56
00:05:29,290 --> 00:05:32,670
Would you be able to sacrifice your
flesh and blood for someone else?

57
00:05:33,920 --> 00:05:36,830
S-Sacrifice Rafilia? How could I?!

58
00:05:36,920 --> 00:05:41,170
Right? I knew you'd understand.

59
00:05:41,460 --> 00:05:44,210
In exchange for keeping quiet
about your condemnation,

60
00:05:44,290 --> 00:05:48,250
the royal family has demanded
our precious daughter, Ellen.

61
00:05:49,000 --> 00:05:50,920
What is this all about?

62
00:05:51,420 --> 00:05:56,210
Aria, you pledged a false oath before the
goddess on your marriage papers, didn't you?

63
00:05:56,290 --> 00:05:57,790
A false oath?

64
00:05:57,880 --> 00:06:02,330
When you signed them, you were thinking
of someone other than Sauvel, weren't you?

65
00:06:03,500 --> 00:06:08,790
That thorny bruise on your wrist
is Goddess Vár's condemnation.

66
00:06:09,080 --> 00:06:12,540
What?! C-Condemnation?

67
00:06:13,250 --> 00:06:17,500
It's proof of the sin of swearing
a false oath before the goddess.

68
00:06:18,540 --> 00:06:19,880
Sin?

69
00:06:19,960 --> 00:06:23,960
Do you not love my brother?
Were just you toying with him?!

70
00:06:24,080 --> 00:06:25,710
N-No!

71
00:06:25,790 --> 00:06:27,040
Don't play dumb with me!

72
00:06:27,500 --> 00:06:29,040
Wait, dear.

73
00:06:30,000 --> 00:06:33,080
The bruise is still faint.

74
00:06:33,710 --> 00:06:37,920
This probably means she does love Sauvel.

75
00:06:38,000 --> 00:06:39,460
Then what's the meaning of this?

76
00:06:39,920 --> 00:06:42,830
Aria, I think you know.

77
00:06:44,540 --> 00:06:47,580
This is a warning from Big Sister Vár.

78
00:06:48,380 --> 00:06:51,960
Do not let your eyes wander.
Wholeheartedly love Sauvel.

79
00:06:52,250 --> 00:06:56,670
If you proceed as you have been,
it is down the path to ruin.

80
00:06:56,920 --> 00:06:57,960
What?

81
00:07:03,630 --> 00:07:06,960
There. Now no one else will
be able see your bruise.

82
00:07:07,330 --> 00:07:10,420
However, it is visible to you.

83
00:07:10,750 --> 00:07:14,920
It will only disappear once
you love Sauvel with all your heart.

84
00:07:15,790 --> 00:07:20,000
Listen well. You are to tell
no one of this. Not even Sauvel.

85
00:07:25,830 --> 00:07:31,880
With Agiel gone, I thought that
Uncle Sauvel could finally be happy...

86
00:07:32,710 --> 00:07:36,580
I think this is the first time I've
ever seen my father so angry.

87
00:07:38,170 --> 00:07:40,790
But a declaration of war, eh,
Mr. Blackheart?

88
00:07:41,790 --> 00:07:42,920
Very well!

89
00:07:43,000 --> 00:07:46,000
In that case, it's time I learned
about our enemy!

90
00:07:57,000 --> 00:07:58,040
Father.

91
00:07:58,960 --> 00:08:02,830
Why is it that the royal family
cannot form a pact with the spirits?

92
00:08:03,960 --> 00:08:08,460
Not only can we not form pacts,
we cannot even approach them.

93
00:08:09,040 --> 00:08:12,330
The reason for this remains
a long-standing mystery.

94
00:08:13,670 --> 00:08:14,710
However...

95
00:08:21,130 --> 00:08:22,880
What should I do?

96
00:08:23,130 --> 00:08:25,830
They told me not to tell Sauvel, but...

97
00:08:25,920 --> 00:08:29,460
Still, there's what my sister-in-law said.

98
00:08:29,540 --> 00:08:33,580
If I'm to love Sauvel with all my heart...

99
00:08:34,040 --> 00:08:37,670
C-Coming! I'll be right there.

100
00:08:40,000 --> 00:08:41,630
Are you all right, Aria?

101
00:08:41,710 --> 00:08:46,380
Yes. I'm sorry for keeping everyone waiting.

102
00:08:46,460 --> 00:08:50,290
No worries. Besides that, how are you feeling?

103
00:08:51,290 --> 00:08:52,960
You don't look well.

104
00:08:53,540 --> 00:08:54,630
Are you all right?

105
00:08:54,710 --> 00:08:56,790
Yes, I'm fine now.

106
00:08:56,880 --> 00:09:00,500
But may I stay here for just a little longer?

107
00:09:00,790 --> 00:09:02,210
Of course you may.

108
00:09:04,130 --> 00:09:05,290
Sauvel.

109
00:09:11,790 --> 00:09:17,460
Milady, if you make too much of a mess,
your mother and father will scold you.

110
00:09:17,750 --> 00:09:21,420
It'll be fine, Vint.
I'm collecting intel on our enemy.

111
00:09:21,670 --> 00:09:23,380
They wouldn't get angry about this.

112
00:09:23,460 --> 00:09:25,130
No, I won't <i>let</i> them get angry!

113
00:09:26,960 --> 00:09:30,460
If there is anything you'd like
to know, you need but ask.

114
00:09:31,130 --> 00:09:34,130
I believe you'll find what
you're looking for sooner that way.

115
00:09:34,500 --> 00:09:38,880
Then do you know anything about the
curse the spirits placed on the royal family?

116
00:09:39,830 --> 00:09:41,920
How do you know about that, milady?

117
00:09:42,420 --> 00:09:45,380
I saw a black mist
coming off the royal family.

118
00:09:45,790 --> 00:09:49,880
And when I asked my mother,
she said it was a curse by the spirits.

119
00:09:49,960 --> 00:09:52,630
Goodness. You can already see that?

120
00:09:53,420 --> 00:09:55,380
Mother said the same thing.

121
00:09:57,130 --> 00:10:01,960
Still, I don't know much about it,
and I feel it's yet too soon for you, milady.

122
00:10:02,080 --> 00:10:06,540
We're past that. I told you,
I'm collecting intelligence on our enemy.

123
00:10:07,040 --> 00:10:09,040
What do you mean by "our enemy"?

124
00:10:09,130 --> 00:10:13,330
Mr. Blackheart... Oh, I mean, King Ravisel.

125
00:10:13,420 --> 00:10:15,540
He has leverage on the Vankreift family

126
00:10:15,630 --> 00:10:19,170
and is using it to summon me and my
father to the castle against our will.

127
00:10:21,710 --> 00:10:25,750
Those unrepentant bastards!
They would again dare to...

128
00:10:26,630 --> 00:10:28,250
Vint!

129
00:10:31,580 --> 00:10:33,250
Milady, my apolo—

130
00:10:36,170 --> 00:10:37,710
So you <i>do</i> know something?

131
00:10:41,250 --> 00:10:43,630
I absolutely have to find out.

132
00:10:45,080 --> 00:10:48,170
Understood. I shall tell you.

133
00:10:49,880 --> 00:10:54,500
It all happened... two hundred years
ago during the Monster Tempest.

134
00:10:55,040 --> 00:10:58,170
The measures taken by the king at the
time to fight the tempest

135
00:10:58,250 --> 00:11:00,420
are what begot the curse.

136
00:11:00,500 --> 00:11:02,330
What in the world did he do?

137
00:11:02,420 --> 00:11:07,790
The royal family demanded the spirit queen
come out to turn the tides of battle.

138
00:11:07,880 --> 00:11:12,250
Naturally, we couldn't
just give into his demand.

139
00:11:13,080 --> 00:11:17,630
Our queen would never lend her powers
to humans for something like that.

140
00:11:17,960 --> 00:11:22,380
However, the fed-up king decided
he'd resort to a forbidden act.

141
00:11:23,420 --> 00:11:24,830
A forbidden act?

142
00:11:31,250 --> 00:11:34,250
Ellen, I'm coming in!

143
00:11:35,170 --> 00:11:36,960
We're home, Ellen.

144
00:11:37,040 --> 00:11:39,330
It's gotten very late.

145
00:11:39,670 --> 00:11:43,210
I'm not angry at you for breaking
our promise, so come here.

146
00:11:47,670 --> 00:11:49,670
What's the matter, Ellen?

147
00:11:50,210 --> 00:11:53,080
Mother, Vint told me everything.

148
00:11:53,170 --> 00:11:54,750
Oh? About what?

149
00:11:55,580 --> 00:11:57,460
The royal family's curse.

150
00:11:59,710 --> 00:12:02,500
I see. So you asked him, did you?

151
00:12:02,580 --> 00:12:04,460
You're a kind child.

152
00:12:04,540 --> 00:12:09,630
I haven't told you because I thought
you might try to break the curse.

153
00:12:10,210 --> 00:12:13,750
But we spirits will never
forgive the royal family.

154
00:12:13,830 --> 00:12:17,080
The tragedy and the cries of our kin...

155
00:12:18,130 --> 00:12:20,290
Please understand.

156
00:12:21,880 --> 00:12:23,920
I am not so kind.

157
00:12:25,710 --> 00:12:27,630
In fact, I find the royal family impudent

158
00:12:27,710 --> 00:12:31,790
for continuing to live so comfortably,
oblivious to the cause of the curse.

159
00:12:32,250 --> 00:12:33,880
Ellen, dear...

160
00:12:36,830 --> 00:12:37,880
I'm sorry.

161
00:12:38,880 --> 00:12:41,170
Why are you apologizing, Father?

162
00:12:41,250 --> 00:12:44,040
I have human blood as well.

163
00:12:44,130 --> 00:12:48,420
And Grammie, Pawpaw,
Uncle Sauvel, Uncle Alberto...

164
00:12:48,500 --> 00:12:51,670
I love everyone from the
Vankreift family too!

165
00:12:52,000 --> 00:12:57,170
Besides, I am your daughter.
I am the daughter of both of you.

166
00:12:57,250 --> 00:13:01,670
And I'm proud of that. There's no reason
for you to worry, Father.

167
00:13:03,670 --> 00:13:05,920
What cannot be allowed to stand
is the royal family

168
00:13:06,000 --> 00:13:11,040
still trying to use the spirits' power
while unaware of the gravity of their sin.

169
00:13:18,670 --> 00:13:20,500
That's my girl!

170
00:13:20,630 --> 00:13:22,330
I don't want to hear that, Father.

171
00:13:22,420 --> 00:13:23,460
Why not?!

172
00:13:24,000 --> 00:13:26,290
You were watching, weren't you, Ellen?

173
00:13:26,880 --> 00:13:30,330
Yes. You mean Mr. Blackheart's
declaration of war, right?

174
00:13:30,420 --> 00:13:31,960
I say bring on the challenge!

175
00:13:34,460 --> 00:13:36,250
You certainly are Rovel's child!

176
00:13:36,330 --> 00:13:38,130
Mother, I don't want to hear that!

177
00:13:38,210 --> 00:13:39,420
Again, why not?!

178
00:13:40,170 --> 00:13:43,250
I think my daughter's in her rebellious phase.

179
00:13:43,710 --> 00:13:46,040
By the way, what happened afterward?

180
00:13:46,130 --> 00:13:50,630
That Aria... She went
and told Sauvel of her sin.

181
00:13:50,710 --> 00:13:51,670
What?

182
00:13:51,750 --> 00:13:54,790
After Rovel told her not to and everything.

183
00:13:54,880 --> 00:13:56,670
What a foolish girl, don't you think?

184
00:13:56,750 --> 00:14:01,630
And so, Sauvel ended up calling off
the reception party midway.

185
00:14:02,170 --> 00:14:04,250
My, the house was in quite an uproar.

186
00:14:04,330 --> 00:14:08,960
I was so furious that I told him I
won't be coming home for a while.

187
00:14:09,210 --> 00:14:12,790
Mother and Roren did want to see you, but...

188
00:14:12,880 --> 00:14:17,540
I see. Poor Uncle Sauvel.

189
00:14:17,830 --> 00:14:18,880
Yeah.

190
00:14:18,960 --> 00:14:22,040
Father, would it be all right
if I go visit Grammie

191
00:14:22,130 --> 00:14:25,080
and the others when Aunt Aria isn't there?

192
00:14:26,250 --> 00:14:30,170
Yes, but I just declared
I wouldn't be returning,

193
00:14:30,250 --> 00:14:31,960
so it's a little hard to visit after that.

194
00:14:32,080 --> 00:14:36,710
I want to see Grammie and Pawpaw
and Uncle Sauvel and Uncle Alberto!

195
00:14:36,790 --> 00:14:39,580
I really want to see them!

196
00:14:39,670 --> 00:14:42,790
Let's go! Let's go tomorrow!

197
00:14:42,880 --> 00:14:44,250
Well, that's really sudden.

198
00:14:44,330 --> 00:14:46,750
Yes. It's urgent.

199
00:14:50,790 --> 00:14:53,330
You could have just gone
directly into the mansion.

200
00:14:53,420 --> 00:14:55,880
I told you, this is kind of hard for me.

201
00:14:58,040 --> 00:15:00,170
Grammie!

202
00:15:00,250 --> 00:15:05,170
Oh, my sweet Ellen, I was so lonely!

203
00:15:05,250 --> 00:15:08,830
Lady Isabella, you're
suffocating the young lady.

204
00:15:09,130 --> 00:15:11,750
My! I'm very sorry, Ellen, dear.

205
00:15:11,830 --> 00:15:14,210
I was just so happy to see you.

206
00:15:14,290 --> 00:15:15,500
Grammie...

207
00:15:15,750 --> 00:15:18,670
It has been too long, Lady Ellen.

208
00:15:18,750 --> 00:15:20,880
Pawpaw, I missed you!

209
00:15:22,670 --> 00:15:28,830
My, just when I thought things were looking
brighter for the house... This again.

210
00:15:28,920 --> 00:15:30,460
It's all right.

211
00:15:31,210 --> 00:15:32,380
Don't cry!

212
00:15:32,710 --> 00:15:34,210
I'm sorry.

213
00:15:34,290 --> 00:15:39,170
Don't misunderstand.
I'm happy just to have you here, Ellen.

214
00:15:39,790 --> 00:15:41,290
Grammie...

215
00:15:43,170 --> 00:15:44,170
Did you need something?

216
00:15:44,250 --> 00:15:46,040
Uncle Sauvel!

217
00:15:49,290 --> 00:15:51,540
Nice to meet you, Aunt Aria.

218
00:15:51,630 --> 00:15:54,830
I am Rovel's daughter, Ellen.

219
00:15:57,250 --> 00:15:58,420
Greet her back.

220
00:16:00,880 --> 00:16:04,130
Brother, was there something
you needed to say to Aria?

221
00:16:04,210 --> 00:16:06,540
I don't. Ellen does.

222
00:16:12,420 --> 00:16:14,210
What did you want to talk about?

223
00:16:14,290 --> 00:16:16,580
Well, it's not really a talk.

224
00:16:17,080 --> 00:16:18,080
It's a warning.

225
00:16:18,170 --> 00:16:19,210
What?

226
00:16:20,170 --> 00:16:24,710
Ellen is Rafilia's age, but as you
can see, she's no ordinary child.

227
00:16:25,170 --> 00:16:27,040
Take what she says seriously.

228
00:16:28,210 --> 00:16:29,330
Understood.

229
00:16:31,040 --> 00:16:33,330
My mother was mindful
of Uncle Sauvel's feelings

230
00:16:33,420 --> 00:16:36,630
and cast a spell so that only
you could see the proof of your sin.

231
00:16:37,380 --> 00:16:43,580
Yet you disobeyed my father's order not
to tell anyone and revealed this to my uncle.

232
00:16:43,670 --> 00:16:45,250
Th-That was because...

233
00:16:45,920 --> 00:16:49,500
Your mother told me to love Sauvel, so...

234
00:16:49,920 --> 00:16:53,170
Should I really be keeping secrets
from the one I love?

235
00:16:53,250 --> 00:16:56,330
Did you think Uncle Sauvel would
forgive you if you told him?

236
00:16:57,330 --> 00:17:02,920
Who would forgive someone for confessing that
they thought of someone else at the altar?

237
00:17:03,000 --> 00:17:06,130
It's an insult to the Vankreift family.

238
00:17:08,960 --> 00:17:10,130
That's right.

239
00:17:11,170 --> 00:17:17,170
Sauvel told you about Agiel,
yet you're doing the same thing.

240
00:17:17,250 --> 00:17:18,460
That's not true!

241
00:17:18,750 --> 00:17:21,500
I'm going to be part of the family!

242
00:17:21,580 --> 00:17:25,460
So it's only natural to seek
my new brother's favor!

243
00:17:25,880 --> 00:17:29,040
You already acknowledged that
your feelings are impure.

244
00:17:29,670 --> 00:17:32,290
That is why Big Sister Vár condemned you.

245
00:17:33,670 --> 00:17:37,000
And the king knows it.

246
00:17:38,500 --> 00:17:39,750
I'm sorry.

247
00:17:39,830 --> 00:17:43,380
No, it's not your fault, Uncle Sauvel.

248
00:17:44,000 --> 00:17:47,630
Aunt Aria, the Vankreift family,
beloved by the spirits,

249
00:17:47,710 --> 00:17:50,580
is indispensable to the royal family.

250
00:17:50,670 --> 00:17:55,040
Even I know that. That's only obvious
with my brother dearest the hero here.

251
00:17:55,380 --> 00:17:56,880
It's more than that!

252
00:17:57,750 --> 00:18:00,080
The reason the royal family dogs us so

253
00:18:00,170 --> 00:18:01,920
isn't because of my father's title.

254
00:18:02,000 --> 00:18:04,500
Above all else, they need his power.

255
00:18:05,500 --> 00:18:09,210
His power is so great that it
keeps neighboring nations in check.

256
00:18:09,290 --> 00:18:15,130
However, your selfish actions risk
stripping our kingdom of its power.

257
00:18:15,210 --> 00:18:18,580
I don't understand at all.
What are you talking about?

258
00:18:18,670 --> 00:18:23,290
Because of you, my father declared
he wouldn't return here for fear

259
00:18:23,380 --> 00:18:25,630
of straining your relationship
with Uncle Sauvel.

260
00:18:25,710 --> 00:18:27,420
And what of it?

261
00:18:28,170 --> 00:18:31,130
If my father, a key part
of our military might,

262
00:18:31,210 --> 00:18:33,210
were to disappear from the human world...

263
00:18:33,290 --> 00:18:34,960
Get to the point!

264
00:18:35,250 --> 00:18:37,960
Perhaps the royal family will see it this way:

265
00:18:38,080 --> 00:18:43,670
"If the nuisance were gone,
the hero may return."

266
00:18:44,330 --> 00:18:46,710
"Getting rid of the nuisance
will fix everything."

267
00:18:47,040 --> 00:18:49,080
The... nuisance?

268
00:18:49,460 --> 00:18:51,460
I'm talking about you, Aunt Aria!

269
00:18:52,210 --> 00:18:53,420
Me?

270
00:18:54,250 --> 00:18:56,330
Why do you think the royal family

271
00:18:56,420 --> 00:18:59,580
attended Uncle's wedding after
what happened with Agiel?

272
00:19:01,170 --> 00:19:03,380
It was to assess your worth.

273
00:19:03,460 --> 00:19:04,830
That can't be...

274
00:19:04,920 --> 00:19:08,750
Not only to see whether you are
worthy of the Vankreift family,

275
00:19:08,830 --> 00:19:12,670
but also to determine your importance
and value as a person.

276
00:19:12,750 --> 00:19:17,130
And yet you've done nothing but drag us down!

277
00:19:17,960 --> 00:19:21,210
No... No!

278
00:19:22,210 --> 00:19:27,540
Aria, there are many women who fall
in love with Rovel at first sight.

279
00:19:27,880 --> 00:19:31,830
It may have been inevitable
that you were one of them.

280
00:19:32,250 --> 00:19:38,330
Still, Sauvel was so happy
to finally be able to marry you.

281
00:19:38,630 --> 00:19:41,210
I do love Sauvel!

282
00:19:41,290 --> 00:19:47,540
Then cease your impure feelings for my father
that only put your life at risk.

283
00:19:48,960 --> 00:19:50,750
Listen carefully, Aunt Aria.

284
00:19:51,500 --> 00:19:56,170
If you dare pursue my father,
my mother and I will show no mercy.

285
00:19:56,250 --> 00:20:01,380
We will slowly and certainly crush you.

286
00:20:03,540 --> 00:20:05,580
You've been warned!

287
00:20:14,880 --> 00:20:19,380
Despite everything, I...
I want to believe in Aria.

288
00:20:25,130 --> 00:20:29,170
I'm sorry for forcing an eight-year-old
to say such things.

289
00:20:29,250 --> 00:20:32,830
No, I was the one who
couldn't bear to keep silent.

290
00:20:32,920 --> 00:20:34,960
I'm sorry for acting out of line.

291
00:20:35,040 --> 00:20:40,130
If it weren't for you, Ellen,
I think this family would've fallen apart.

292
00:20:40,750 --> 00:20:42,500
Truly, thank you.

293
00:20:43,460 --> 00:20:44,750
Uncle...

294
00:20:46,750 --> 00:20:51,210
Now then, we should be off to the castle,
shouldn't we, Father?

295
00:20:51,290 --> 00:20:54,630
Yeah, you're right. Man, I don't wanna...

296
00:20:54,920 --> 00:20:59,330
If that's the case,
you need a new dress, Ellen!

297
00:20:59,420 --> 00:21:01,830
Rovel, we need something for you too!

298
00:21:02,500 --> 00:21:06,580
Roren, immediately call in
our best seamstress!

299
00:21:06,670 --> 00:21:09,130
Yes, milady! I'll make
the arrangements right away.

300
00:21:09,210 --> 00:21:11,920
Things are going to get busy!

301
00:21:12,250 --> 00:21:16,460
I'm sorry. My mother always wanted a daughter.

302
00:21:17,040 --> 00:21:19,960
That's why she goes so overboard.

303
00:21:20,040 --> 00:21:22,670
I see. In that case...

304
00:21:22,750 --> 00:21:26,420
Makeup artists assemble!

305
00:21:27,460 --> 00:21:32,830
I think you should share
this fate with me, Uncle Sauvel.

306
00:21:33,170 --> 00:21:34,170
Wha...?!

307
00:21:34,250 --> 00:21:39,250
If you don't want to get dragged into this,
Father, please restrain Uncle Sauvel.

308
00:21:39,330 --> 00:21:40,630
You got it, Ellen.

309
00:21:40,710 --> 00:21:41,670
What?!

310
00:21:41,750 --> 00:21:43,580
Forgive me, Sauvel!

311
00:21:43,710 --> 00:21:44,960
B-Brother?!

312
00:21:45,080 --> 00:21:46,670
I cannot argue with my daughter.

313
00:21:46,750 --> 00:21:48,290
Uncle Sauvel!

314
00:21:49,540 --> 00:21:51,290
Prepare yourself!

315
00:21:57,580 --> 00:22:01,040
Hmm, h-how does it look?

316
00:22:01,380 --> 00:22:03,880
You look wonderful without a beard, Uncle!

317
00:22:03,960 --> 00:22:04,960
Yeah.

318
00:22:07,250 --> 00:22:13,880
I thought if we make him look cool, maybe
Aunt Aria won't have eyes for anyone else.

319
00:22:13,960 --> 00:22:15,880
And that's why you wanted to see Sauvel?

320
00:22:17,580 --> 00:22:20,290
I see. What a great idea!

321
00:22:21,170 --> 00:22:24,630
TRANSLATION: YUKARI MURASE-LOUDEN

322
00:22:24,920 --> 00:22:28,330
EDITING: RILEY DALTON

323
00:22:28,710 --> 00:22:31,830
QUALITY CHECK: ASHLEY BARBOZA
